Golay complementary matrices (GCM) have recently attracted significant attention due to their potential applications in omnidirectional precoding. In this paper, we introduce a novel construction method for GCMs, termed the "direct" construction. This approach combines two GCMs of size $2\times N$ (where $N$ is any positive integer) using a specific identity matrix and its conjugate. We demonstrate that this direct construction yields a new GCM of dimensions $M\times (N(M-1))$ derived from the initial pair of matrices of size $2\times N$. Furthermore, we establish an equivalence between this direct construction and a previously known method by Golay, showing that the direct construction for two matrices can be achieved via the direct construction of a single matrix coupled with a permutation. Finally, we utilize the direct construction to identify a pair of 7x7 GCMs, which subsequently enables a new set of seven Golay complementary matrices of 21x21 dimensions.

